                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Where can birds find water to drink in the hottest months in the hottest desert?\n\nHelpful knowledge: Deserts are hot and dry regions with little rainfall. Many desert animals have adapted to survive in these harsh conditions by conserving water and finding alternative sources of hydration.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How do birds survive in the desert?\n2. What are some common sources of water for desert animals?\n3. Which of the given options are likely sources of water for birds in the desert?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Birds in the desert have adapted to conserve water by reducing their activity during the hottest parts of the day, panting to cool down, and excreting concentrated urine to retain water.\n2. Common sources of water for desert animals include underground springs, cacti, succulent plants, and insects.\n3. Of the given options, spiked plants (option D) are the most likely source of water for birds in the desert. Some desert plants, such as the saguaro cactus, have spines that collect moisture from the air and funnel it down to the base of the plant where animals can drink from it.",
