                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by fire giving off light?\n\nProfessor: Sure, when something is on fire, it produces light as a result of the chemical reaction that is taking place.\n\nStudent: Can you give me an example of this?\n\nProfessor: Yes, one example would be a lit candle in a window signaling to someone.\n\nStudent: How does the candle produce light?\n\nProfessor: The heat from the flame causes the wax to melt and vaporize, which then reacts with oxygen in the air to produce a flame. The flame produces light as a result of the energy released during the chemical reaction.\n\nStudent: What about the other options?\n\nProfessor: Another example would be a match being lit to light a cigarette. The heat from the match causes the chemicals in the match head to react, producing a flame that gives off light. An oven being preheated and the pilot light being lit also produces light, but it's not necessarily a result of fire. And a fire that was put out to send smoke signals doesn't produce light at all.",
