                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Define erosion\nErosion is the process of wearing away or breaking down of materials such as soil, rock, or sediment by natural forces such as wind, water, or ice.\n\nStep 2: Identify the options\nA) soil\nB) fish\nC) rocks\nD) weather\n\nStep 3: Determine which option(s) can cause erosion\nA) Soil: Yes, soil erosion is a common type of erosion caused by water, wind, or human activities such as farming or construction.\nB) Fish: No, fish do not cause erosion.\nC) Rocks: Yes, rock erosion can occur due to weathering, which is the breakdown of rocks by natural forces such as wind, water, or ice.\nD) Weather: Yes, weather is a major cause of erosion as it can cause physical and chemical changes to materials such as soil, rock, or sediment.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is D) weather.",
