                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Erosion is the act of something being worn away. So, it's caused by an agent that can wear away something. \n\nA) Soil can cause erosion if it's loose and dry and there's wind. The wind will pick up the soil and deposit it somewhere else. \nB) Fish can't cause erosion. \nC) Rocks can cause erosion if they're being hit by water or wind. The water or wind will wear away the rock over time. \nD) Weather can cause erosion if it's windy or rainy. The wind will pick up loose soil and the rain will wash away soil.",
