                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the solution to power electromagnets that are not working?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Electromagnets are not working due to difficulty in powering them.\n- To make them work, we need to find a solution.\n- The options given are A) run wire through currants, B) run a continuous current, C) run around the wire, and D) currently run wire through.\n- Option A does not make sense as it is unclear what is meant by \"currants\" and how running wire through them would power the electromagnets.\n- Option B seems like a plausible solution as electromagnets require a continuous flow of current to work.\n- Option C does not make sense as it is unclear what is meant by \"run around the wire\" and how it would power the electromagnets.\n- Option D is similar to option A and does not make sense.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is B) run a continuous current.\n\nAnswer: B) run a continuous current.",
                        "answers": [
