                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: There are various types of objects used to hold sheets of paper together, such as paper clips, staples, binder clips, and magnetic clips.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are paper clips made of?\n2. What are staples made of?\n3. What are binder clips made of?\n4. What are magnetic clips made of?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Paper clips are typically made of steel wire coated with plastic or vinyl.\n2. Staples are usually made of thin wire, often galvanized or stainless steel.\n3. Binder clips are made of metal, usually steel or nickel-plated steel, with two or more wire loops that can be pressed together to hold papers.\n4. Magnetic clips have a metal clip attached to a magnet, which can hold papers together without puncturing or damaging them.\n\nOriginal question: What types of objects are often used to hold sheets of paper together?\n\nAnswer: Various types of objects are used to hold sheets of paper together, including paper clips, staples, binder clips, and magnetic clips. These objects can be made of different materials, such as steel wire, galvanized or stainless steel, metal, and magnets. They are not necessarily large, wooden, ferromagnetic, or electronic.",
