                        "cot": "To be visible while running at night, I need to use a reflector. A reflector is a material that reflects light back to its source. This makes me visible to drivers and other people who might be around. \n\nOption A, a black shirt, is not a good choice for a reflector because black absorbs light and does not reflect it. \n\nOption B, kitchen foil, is a good choice for a reflector because it is shiny and reflective. I can cut a small piece of foil and attach it to my clothing or shoes to make myself visible. \n\nOption C, sunglasses, are not a good choice for a reflector because they are designed to block light, not reflect it. \n\nOption D, a megaphone, is not a good choice for a reflector because it is not reflective at all. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Kitchen foil.",
