                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain to me what a reflector is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, a reflector is a material or object that reflects light back to its source. It helps increase visibility and can be useful for safety purposes, especially when running at night.\n\nStudent: Okay, so which of the options would work as a reflector?\n\nProfessor: Out of the options given, the only one that would work as a reflector is kitchen foil. It is a shiny material that reflects light well.\n\nStudent: Why wouldn't a black shirt work as a reflector?\n\nProfessor: A black shirt would actually have the opposite effect of a reflector. It absorbs light and doesn't reflect it back, making it harder for others to see you at night.\n\nStudent: And what about sunglasses?\n\nProfessor: Sunglasses are meant to protect your eyes from the sun, but they don't reflect light back to its source. They wouldn't be very helpful as a reflector.\n\nStudent: And a megaphone?\n\nProfessor: A megaphone is not a reflective material or object. It is used to amplify sound, not reflect light. So, it wouldn't work as a reflector either.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that to me, Professor. I think I understand now.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome, always happy to help. Stay safe on your night runs!",
