                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define echolocation\n2. Identify how echolocation works\n3. Determine what information echolocation can provide\n4. Match the information provided by echolocation to the options given in the question\n5. Choose the correct answer\n\nAnswer: B) shape\n\nExplanation:\n1. Echolocation is a biological sonar system used by animals such as bats, dolphins, and whales to navigate and locate prey.\n2. Echolocation works by emitting high-frequency sound waves and listening for the echoes that bounce back off of objects in the environment.\n3. Echolocation can provide information about the location, direction, and movement of objects in the environment, as well as their texture and density.\n4. The options given in the question are distance, shape, size, and temperature. Echolocation can provide information about distance, but it cannot provide precise measurements of size or temperature. However, echolocation can provide detailed information about the shape of objects based on the echoes that bounce back.\n5. Therefore, the correct answer is B) shape.",
