                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) nutrients.\n\nCellular respiration is the process by which cells convert nutrients into energy. This process occurs in the mitochondria of the cell. The nutrients that are consumed during cellular respiration include glucose, amino acids, and fatty acids. These nutrients are broken down through a series of chemical reactions that release energy in the form of ATP (adenosine triphosphate). Water and gas are not consumed during cellular respiration, although oxygen is required as a reactant in the process. Therefore, the correct answer is B) nutrients.",
