                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Cellular respiration is the process by which cells convert nutrients into energy in the form of ATP (adenosine triphosphate). This process occurs in the mitochondria of the cell.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is cellular respiration?\n2. What is the role of nutrients in cellular respiration?\n3. Where does cellular respiration occur in the cell?\n4. What is the end product of cellular respiration?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Cellular respiration is the process by which cells convert nutrients into energy in the form of ATP.\n2. Nutrients are consumed by the cell during cellular respiration to provide the necessary energy for the process.\n3. Cellular respiration occurs in the mitochondria of the cell.\n4. The end product of cellular respiration is ATP, which is used by the cell for energy. \n\nAnswer to original question: Cellular respiration is when energy is produced in a cell by consumption of nutrients.",
