                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand what a full moon is and how it occurs.\n2. Determine the average length of a lunar cycle.\n3. Calculate how many lunar cycles occur in a month.\n4. Determine how many of those lunar cycles result in a full moon.\n5. Use the answer from step 4 to select the correct option.\n\nAnswer:\n1. A full moon occurs when the moon is on the opposite side of the Earth from the sun, with the Earth in between. This alignment causes the entire illuminated side of the moon to face the Earth, making it appear as a complete circle.\n2. The average length of a lunar cycle is 29.5 days.\n3. There are approximately 12.37 lunar cycles in a month (365.25 days in a year divided by 29.5 days per lunar cycle).\n4. On average, there is one full moon per lunar cycle. Therefore, there is approximately one full moon per month.\n5. The answer is C) once.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "fff17068-4eda-4649-ac64-47d2783923c3",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
