                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: How often does a full moon occur in a month on average?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A full moon occurs when the moon is on the opposite side of the Earth from the sun, so that its entire illuminated side is facing us.\n- The lunar cycle, or the time it takes for the moon to go through all its phases (including full moon), is about 29.5 days.\n- This means that there can be at most one full moon per month, since the length of a month is usually either 30 or 31 days.\n- However, sometimes there can be two full moons in a month, which is called a \"blue moon\". This happens when the first full moon occurs early in the month (usually within the first two days) and the second full moon occurs at the end of the month (usually within the last two days).\n- Therefore, the answer is A) twice, but with the caveat that this only happens occasionally and not every month. On average, there is one full moon per month.",
