                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the properties of light.\n2. Understand the concept of reflection.\n3. Determine the type of object that can reflect light.\n\nAnswer: \nThe correct answer is C) item that reflects. Light is a form of electromagnetic radiation that travels in straight lines until it interacts with an object. When light hits an object, it can either be absorbed, transmitted, or reflected. Reflection occurs when light bounces off an object and changes direction. Therefore, an object that can reflect light is required for light to bounce off of it.",
