                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) item that reflects.\n\nLight can bounce off of any object, but it will only reflect off of an item that has a reflective surface. This means that the surface of the object is smooth and shiny enough to reflect the light waves that hit it. Examples of items that reflect light include mirrors, polished metal surfaces, and glass. Therefore, the correct answer is C) item that reflects. \n\nOption A) tadpole is incorrect because tadpoles are living organisms and do not have a reflective surface. \n\nOption B) any object is partially correct, but it does not fully answer the question because not all objects have a reflective surface. \n\nOption D) black hole is incorrect because black holes do not reflect light. In fact, they absorb all light that comes near them, which is why they appear black.",
                        "answers": [
