                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Light is a form of electromagnetic radiation that travels in straight lines until it interacts with matter. When light interacts with matter, it can be absorbed, transmitted, or reflected.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What does it mean for an object to reflect light?\n2. Can all objects reflect light?\n3. What types of objects are good reflectors of light?\n\nAnswers:\n1. When an object reflects light, it means that the light bounces off the surface of the object and changes direction.\n2. No, not all objects can reflect light. Some objects absorb light, while others transmit it.\n3. Objects that are smooth and shiny, such as mirrors, metals, and glass, are good reflectors of light. Rough and dull surfaces, such as paper and fabric, are not good reflectors of light.\n\nAnswer to original question: C) item that reflects. Light bounces off of objects that are able to reflect it, such as mirrors, metals, and glass.",
                        "answers": [
