                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) adding sand.\n\nTo reduce ice buildup on a sidewalk, adding sand is the most effective solution. This is because sand provides traction and helps to prevent slips and falls. \n\nAdding salt can also be effective, as it lowers the freezing point of water and causes the ice to melt. However, salt can be harmful to plants and animals, and can also damage concrete and metal surfaces over time. \n\nAdding litter or water will not reduce ice buildup and may actually make the situation worse. Litter can create a hazard by causing people to slip, and water will freeze and create more ice. \n\nTherefore, the best option is to add sand to the sidewalk to provide traction and reduce the risk of slips and falls.",
