                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What can be added to a sidewalk with ice buildup to reduce the ice?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Ice buildup on a sidewalk can be dangerous and slippery.\n- To reduce the ice, something needs to be added to it.\n- Option A suggests adding salt. Salt can lower the freezing point of water, which means it can melt the ice faster. This is a common method used to de-ice sidewalks and roads.\n- Option B suggests adding litter. Litter is unlikely to reduce ice buildup, and may even make the sidewalk more slippery.\n- Option C suggests adding sand. Sand can provide traction on the ice, making it less slippery. This is another common method used to de-ice sidewalks and roads.\n- Option D suggests adding water. Adding water to ice would likely make it worse, as it would freeze and create more ice.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) adding sand.",
