                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Camouflage is a technique used by animals to blend in with their surroundings, making them less visible to predators or prey. This can be used for hunting purposes, as it allows the animal to remain hidden and undetected until it is ready to strike.\n\nA) Water - Some aquatic animals use camouflage to blend in with their surroundings in the water, making it easier for them to hunt prey. For example, certain fish species can change their coloration to match the ocean floor or coral reefs.\n\nB) Trees - Many animals that live in forests or wooded areas use camouflage to blend in with the trees and foliage. This can help them avoid predators or sneak up on prey. For example, a green tree python's coloration allows it to blend in with the leaves and branches of its habitat.\n\nC) Air - Some birds and insects use camouflage to blend in with the sky or clouds, making it difficult for predators to spot them. For example, certain moth species have wings that resemble the color and pattern of tree bark, allowing them to blend in when they are at rest.\n\nD) Meals - This option does not make sense in the context of camouflage for hunting, as animals do not use camouflage to blend in with their meals.\n\nBased on the information above, the correct answer is:\n\nCamouflage can be used by animals for hunting in:\nA) water\nB) trees\nC) air",
                        "answers": [
