                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nPhotosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. This process requires three main ingredients: carbon dioxide (CO2), water (H2O), and sunlight.\n\nOption A is incorrect because argon is an inert gas that does not participate in photosynthesis.\n\nOption B is incorrect because oxygen is produced as a byproduct of photosynthesis, not a required ingredient. Fertilizer may provide nutrients for plant growth, but it is not a direct ingredient in photosynthesis.\n\nOption C is incorrect because cloudy skies may reduce the amount of sunlight available for photosynthesis, but they do not affect the required ingredients.\n\nOption D is correct because it includes the three main ingredients required for photosynthesis: CO2, H2O, and sun rays.",
