                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to understand what instinctual behavior means. Instinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate, meaning it is not learned but rather inherited genetically. It is a behavior that an animal is born with and does not need to be taught.\n\nOption A, dogs rolling over on command, is not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior. Dogs are trained to roll over on command through positive reinforcement.\n\nOption C, birds mimicking human speech, is also not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior. Birds learn to mimic human speech through exposure and repetition.\n\nOption D, seals clapping for treats from trainers, is also not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior. Seals are trained to clap for treats through positive reinforcement.\n\nOption B, frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs, is an instinctual behavior because it is a behavior that is innate and inherited genetically. Frogs are born with the instinct to return to the pond where they hatched to lay their eggs. This behavior ensures the survival of their offspring by providing them with a suitable environment for growth and development.",
