                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is an example of an instinctual behavior?\n\nTo answer this question, we need to define what an instinctual behavior is. An instinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate and automatic, meaning it is not learned or taught. It is a behavior that is genetically programmed into an organism.\n\nOption A, dogs rolling over on command, is not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior that is taught through training.\n\nOption B, frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs, is an instinctual behavior because it is a behavior that is genetically programmed into the frog. The frog does not need to learn this behavior, it just knows to return to its place of birth to lay eggs.\n\nOption C, birds mimicking human speech, is not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior that is taught through observation and practice.\n\nOption D, seals clapping for treats from trainers, is not an instinctual behavior because it is a learned behavior that is taught through training.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs.",
