                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Instinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate and does not need to be learned.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of instinctual behavior?\n- Instinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate and does not need to be learned.\n\n2. Which of the given behaviors are innate and do not need to be learned?\n- Dogs rolling over on command is a learned behavior, so it is not instinctual.\n- Frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs is an innate behavior, so it is instinctual.\n- Birds mimicking human speech is a learned behavior, so it is not instinctual.\n- Seals clapping for treats from trainers is a learned behavior, so it is not instinctual.\n\nAnswer: The only behavior listed that is instinctual is B) frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs.",
