                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what an instinctual behavior is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, an instinctual behavior is a behavior that an animal is born with and does not need to learn.\n\nStudent: Can you give me an example?\n\nProfessor: Sure, one example is when dogs roll over on command. They do this instinctively without being taught.\n\nStudent: How about the other options? Are they also examples of instinctual behavior?\n\nProfessor: Yes, they are. Frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs is an instinctual behavior. Birds mimicking human speech is also an instinctual behavior. And seals clapping for treats from trainers is also an instinctual behavior.\n\nStudent: How do we know if a behavior is instinctual or learned?\n\nProfessor: We can tell if a behavior is instinctual if it is present in all members of a species, even if they have never seen it before. Learned behaviors, on the other hand, are acquired through experience and are not present in all members of a species.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Thank you for explaining it to me, Professor.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome. Do you have any other questions?",
