                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) various types of animals. \n\nHelpful knowledge: Pollen and seeds are reproductive structures of plants. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are pollen and seeds?\n- Pollen is a fine powdery substance produced by the male reproductive organs of a flower. \n- Seeds are the mature ovules of a flower that contain an embryo and are capable of developing into a new plant. \n\n2. How are pollen and seeds produced?\n- Pollen is produced by the stamen of a flower, which contains the anther where pollen grains are formed. \n- Seeds are produced by the female reproductive organs of a flower, which include the ovary and ovules. \n\n3. What is the role of animals in the production of pollen and seeds?\n- Animals, such as bees, butterflies, birds, and bats, play a crucial role in pollination, which is the transfer of pollen from the male reproductive organs to the female reproductive organs of a flower. \n- Pollination is necessary for the fertilization of the ovules and the production of seeds. \n\nAnswer: Various types of animals produce pollen and seeds through the process of pollination.",
