                        "cot": "To rephrase the question: In which location is there an increased risk of landslides?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Landslides are more likely to occur in areas with steep slopes, loose soil, and heavy rainfall or seismic activity.\n- The desert is generally flat and dry, so it is unlikely to have a heightened threat of landslides.\n- The Andes are a mountain range with steep slopes, so there is a possibility of landslides occurring there.\n- The ocean is a body of water and does not have any land features that could cause landslides.\n- Indiana is a state in the United States that is mostly flat and does not have a history of landslides.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) The Andes.",
