                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The Great Pyramids of Giza are located in Egypt and were built during the Old Kingdom period, around 2500 BCE. They are considered one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a theocratic government?\n2. What was the government system in ancient Egypt during the Old Kingdom period?\n3. Who commissioned the construction of the Great Pyramids?\n4. What was the purpose of the Great Pyramids?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A theocratic government is a system of government in which religious leaders hold the power and make decisions based on religious beliefs and principles.\n2. The government system in ancient Egypt during the Old Kingdom period was a monarchy with a pharaoh as the ruler. The pharaoh was considered a god-king and had absolute power over the people.\n3. The Great Pyramids were commissioned by the pharaohs of the Old Kingdom period, including Khufu, Khafre, and Menkaure.\n4. The purpose of the Great Pyramids was to serve as tombs for the pharaohs and their consorts, as they believed in an afterlife and wanted to ensure their bodies were preserved for it.\n\nConclusion:\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, it can be concluded that the Great Pyramids were not built by a theocratic government, but rather by a monarchy with a pharaoh as the ruler. Therefore, the answer to the original question is B) False.",
