                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define what rainbows are and how they are formed.\n2. Define yin and yang colors.\n3. Determine if rainbows are devoid of color.\n4. Determine if rainbows are made by mixing yin and yang colors.\n5. Use the information gathered to answer the question.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Rainbows are optical and meteorological phenomena that are caused by the reflection, refraction, and dispersion of light in water droplets in the atmosphere.\n2. Yin and yang colors are a concept in traditional Chinese philosophy that refers to the two complementary, yet opposing, forces in the universe. Yin colors are cool and dark, while yang colors are warm and bright. Examples of yin colors include black, blue, and green, while examples of yang colors include red, orange, and yellow.\n3. Rainbows are not devoid of color. In fact, they are made up of a spectrum of colors, including red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet.\n4. Rainbows are not made by mixing yin and yang colors. They are formed by the interaction of light and water droplets in the atmosphere.\n5. Therefore, the answer to the question is B) False.",
