                        "cot": "It is highly unlikely that lobsters can breathe in the desert as they are aquatic animals and require water to survive. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the habitat requirements for lobsters?\n2. What is the definition of a desert?\n3. Can lobsters survive without water?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: Lobsters are marine animals that require saltwater to survive. They are typically found in oceans, seas, and other bodies of saltwater.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2: A desert is a region that receives very little precipitation, typically less than 10 inches per year. Deserts are characterized by their arid climate, lack of vegetation, and extreme temperatures.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3: No, lobsters cannot survive without water. They require water to breathe, as they extract oxygen from the water through their gills. Without water, they would suffocate and die. \n\nTherefore, the answer to the original question is B) False. Lobsters cannot breathe in the desert as they require water to survive.",
