                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Kurt Cobain was the lead singer and guitarist of the band Nirvana, which was active from 1987 to 1994. Nirvana was a prominent band in the grunge music scene, which emerged in the Pacific Northwest region of the United States in the late 1980s and early 1990s.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is grunge music?\n2. Was Nirvana a popular band during Kurt Cobain's lifetime?\n3. Did Kurt Cobain's death have an impact on the popularity of grunge music?\n4. Are there still bands making music in the grunge genre today?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Grunge music is a subgenre of alternative rock that originated in the Pacific Northwest region of the United States in the mid-1980s. It is characterized by its heavy, distorted guitar sound and often bleak or introspective lyrics.\n2. Yes, Nirvana was a very popular band during Kurt Cobain's lifetime. They released three studio albums, all of which were commercially successful and critically acclaimed.\n3. Kurt Cobain's death in 1994 had a significant impact on the popularity of grunge music. Many fans and critics saw him as the voice of a generation and his death was seen as a tragic loss. However, grunge music continued to be popular for a few years after his death, with bands like Pearl Jam and Soundgarden still releasing successful albums.\n4. While grunge music is not as popular as it was in the 1990s, there are still bands making music in the genre today. Some examples include Alice in Chains, Mudhoney, and Screaming Trees. However, these bands are not as commercially successful as Nirvana was during their heyday. \n\nConclusion:\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, the answer to the original question is: True, the grunge music genre did survive after Kurt Cobain's death. While his death had an impact on the popularity of grunge music, there are still bands making music in the genre today.",
