                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine during which season sunset occurs latest in the day, we need to consider the tilt of the Earth's axis and its position in orbit around the sun. \n\nDuring the summer solstice (around June 20-22 in the Northern Hemisphere), the Earth's axis is tilted towards the sun, resulting in longer days and shorter nights. This means that sunset occurs later in the day during the summer season. \n\nDuring the fall equinox (around September 22-23 in the Northern Hemisphere), the Earth's axis is not tilted towards or away from the sun, resulting in roughly equal amounts of daylight and darkness. \n\nDuring the winter solstice (around December 21-22 in the Northern Hemisphere), the Earth's axis is tilted away from the sun, resulting in shorter days and longer nights. This means that sunset occurs earlier in the day during the winter season. \n\nDuring the spring equinox (around March 20-21 in the Northern Hemisphere), the Earth's axis is again not tilted towards or away from the sun, resulting in roughly equal amounts of daylight and darkness. \n\nTherefore, the answer is A) summer, as sunset occurs latest in the day during this season.",
