                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The timing of sunset is affected by the tilt of the Earth's axis and its position in orbit around the sun. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. How does the tilt of the Earth's axis affect the timing of sunset?\n2. How does the Earth's position in orbit around the sun affect the timing of sunset?\n3. Which season has the longest days?\n\nAnswering sub-questions:\n1. The tilt of the Earth's axis causes the sun's rays to hit different parts of the Earth at different angles throughout the year. This affects the amount of daylight and the timing of sunrise and sunset. \n2. The Earth's position in orbit around the sun affects the amount of daylight and the timing of sunrise and sunset. When the Earth is closer to the sun, it moves faster in its orbit and experiences longer days. \n3. Summer has the longest days because the Earth's tilt causes the sun's rays to hit the Northern Hemisphere at a more direct angle, resulting in more daylight hours.\n\nAnswer: A) summer is the season during which sunset occurs latest in the day.",
