                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: The solar system consists of the Sun and the objects that orbit around it, including planets, moons, asteroids, and comets.\n\nStep 2: The planets in the solar system are divided into two groups: the inner planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars) and the outer planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune).\n\nStep 3: The inner planets are also known as the terrestrial planets because they are small, rocky, and have solid surfaces. The outer planets are also known as the gas giants because they are much larger and composed mostly of gas and ice.\n\nStep 4: Based on the above information, we can eliminate options A and D because they are incorrect. The gas planets (outer planets) are not closer to the Sun than the solid planets (inner planets), and the solid planets are not much larger than the gas planets.\n\nStep 5: Option C is also incorrect because the planets are not arranged in order of increasing size. For example, Jupiter is the largest planet in the solar system, but it is not the closest to the Sun.\n\nStep 6: Therefore, the correct answer is B: The solid planets are closer to the Sun. This is because the inner planets (which are solid) are closer to the Sun than the outer planets (which are gas giants).",
