                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you repeat the question, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Which statement is true about the solar system?\n\nStudent: Okay. What are the options?\n\nProfessor: The options are A) The gas planets are closer to the Sun. B) The solid planets are closer to the Sun. C) The planets are arranged in order of increasing size. D) The solid planets are much larger than the gas planets.\n\nStudent: How do we determine which one is true?\n\nProfessor: Well, we can start by eliminating the options that we know are not true. For example, we know that option D is not true because the gas planets are actually much larger than the solid planets.\n\nStudent: Okay, so we can eliminate option D. What about option C?\n\nProfessor: Option C is partially true. The planets are arranged in order of increasing size, but not exactly. For example, Jupiter is the largest planet, but it is not the closest to the Sun.\n\nStudent: So, we can eliminate option C as well. What about options A and B?\n\nProfessor: Options A and B are the only ones left. Do you know the difference between gas planets and solid planets?\n\nStudent: Yes, I do. Gas planets are made up of gases like hydrogen and helium, while solid planets are made up of rocks and metals.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. So, which option do you think is true?\n\nStudent: I think option B is true because the solid planets are closer to the Sun.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Option B is the correct answer. Good job!",
