                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the characteristics of Mars and Jupiter.\n\n- Mars is an inner planet, meaning it is located closer to the Sun than Jupiter.\n- Jupiter is an outer planet, meaning it is located farther from the Sun than Mars.\n\nStep 2: Consider the options given.\n\nA) They are made of the same materials. - This option is not relevant to the relationship between the two planets.\n\nB) They orbit the Sun in opposite directions. - This option is also not relevant to the relationship between the two planets.\n\nC) They have the same orbital periods around the Sun. - This option is incorrect because inner planets like Mars have shorter orbital periods than outer planets like Jupiter.\n\nD) They are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt. - This option correctly describes the relationship between Mars and Jupiter. The asteroid belt is located between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter, so they are indeed located on opposite sides of it.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) They are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt.",
