                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to identify what an inner planet is and what an outer planet is. \n\nAn inner planet is a planet that is closer to the Sun than Earth is. Mercury and Venus are inner planets. \n\nAn outer planet is a planet that is farther from the Sun than Earth is. Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune are outer planets. \n\nNow that we know the difference between inner and outer planets, we can go back to the question. \n\nThe question asks about the relationship between Mars and Jupiter. We are looking for the best description of the relationship between these two planets. \n\nOption A) They are made of the same materials. \nThis is not correct. The composition of inner planets is different from the composition of outer planets. Inner planets are made of rock and outer planets are made of gas. \n\nOption B) They orbit the Sun in opposite directions. \nThis is not correct. All the planets in our solar system orbit the Sun in the same direction. \n\nOption C) They have the same orbital periods around the Sun. \nThis is not correct. The orbital periods of inner planets are shorter than the orbital periods of outer planets. \n\nOption D) They are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt. \nThis is correct. Mars is located on the side of the asteroid belt closer to the Sun, and Jupiter is located on the side of the asteroid belt farther from the Sun.",
