                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The solar system consists of eight planets, four of which are inner planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars) and four of which are outer planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune). The asteroid belt is located between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of an inner planet?\n2. What is the definition of an outer planet?\n3. Which planets are considered inner planets?\n4. Which planets are considered outer planets?\n5. Where is the asteroid belt located?\n6. Are Mars and Jupiter located on the same side or opposite sides of the asteroid belt?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An inner planet is a planet that is located closer to the Sun than the asteroid belt and has a solid, rocky surface.\n2. An outer planet is a planet that is located beyond the asteroid belt and has a gaseous or icy surface.\n3. Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars are considered inner planets.\n4. Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune are considered outer planets.\n5. The asteroid belt is located between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter.\n6. Mars and Jupiter are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt.\n\nConclusion:\nThe correct answer is D) They are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt.",
