                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by inner and outer planets?\n\nProfessor: Sure, inner planets are the planets that are closest to the Sun, which includes Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars. Outer planets are the planets that are farthest from the Sun, which includes Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune.\n\nStudent: Okay, so Mars is an inner planet and Jupiter is an outer planet. What does that tell us about their relationship?\n\nProfessor: Well, it tells us that they are located in different regions of our solar system. But to answer the question, we need to look at the answer choices. Which one do you think is the best answer?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. Can you explain each answer choice?\n\nProfessor: Of course. Option A says that they are made of the same materials, but that's not necessarily true. Option B says that they orbit the Sun in opposite directions, but that's not true either. Option C says that they have the same orbital periods around the Sun, but that's also not true. Option D says that they are located on opposite sides of the asteroid belt, which is true. So the answer is D.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. Thank you for explaining that to me.",
