                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify what gravity is and how it affects objects.\n2. Research the formation of stars and the role of gravity in it.\n3. Analyze the given statements and eliminate the ones that are incorrect.\n4. Choose the statement that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Gravity is a force that attracts objects towards each other. The strength of the force depends on the mass of the objects and the distance between them. Gravity affects the motion of objects in space and can cause them to orbit around each other or collide.\n2. According to current scientific understanding, stars form from clouds of gas and dust in space. These clouds are called nebulae. Gravity plays a crucial role in the formation of stars by causing the gas and dust particles in the nebula to come together and form a dense core. As the core becomes more massive, the gravitational force becomes stronger, causing more gas and dust to be pulled in. Eventually, the core becomes hot and dense enough for nuclear fusion to occur, which ignites the star.\n3. Statement A is incorrect because gravity does not convert solid matter into gases and light energy. Statement C is incorrect because gravity does not cool gases and liquids until they become one solid mass. Statement D is incorrect because gravity does not push rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center.\n4. The statement that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "6e2d8a45-a255-4d29-b55d-9ce4a7cccf17",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
