                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The Moon is a natural satellite of Earth and it takes approximately 27.3 days to complete one orbit around Earth. The Moon's gravitational pull causes tides on Earth.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of revolution?\n2. How does the Moon's revolution around Earth affect Earth's rotation?\n3. How does the Moon's revolution around Earth affect the Moon's appearance in the sky?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Revolution is the movement of an object around another object in a circular or elliptical path.\n2. The Moon's revolution around Earth does not affect Earth's rotation. Earth rotates on its axis independently of the Moon's orbit.\n3. The Moon's revolution around Earth causes it to appear as different shapes during the month. As the Moon orbits Earth, the amount of sunlight reflecting off its surface changes, causing it to appear as different phases, such as full moon, new moon, and crescent moon.",
