                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) planets moving around the Sun in an elliptical pattern is an example of gravity influencing other systems. This is because the force of gravity between the Sun and the planets is what keeps the planets in orbit around the Sun. The gravitational force is what causes the planets to move in an elliptical pattern rather than a straight line. This is a clear example of how gravity influences other systems. \n\nA) Surface water evaporating into the atmosphere is not an example of gravity influencing other systems. While gravity does play a role in the water cycle, it is not the force that causes water to evaporate. Instead, it is the heat from the sun that causes water to evaporate. \n\nC) Glaciers melting because of increasing temperatures is also not an example of gravity influencing other systems. While gravity does play a role in the movement of glaciers, it is not the force that causes them to melt. Instead, it is the increase in temperature that causes the ice to melt. \n\nD) Groundwater moving to the surface in an artesian well is not an example of gravity influencing other systems. While gravity does play a role in the movement of groundwater, it is not the force that causes it to move to the surface in an artesian well. Instead, it is the pressure from the water in the aquifer that causes the water to move to the surface.",
