                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: When a star explodes, it releases a tremendous amount of energy and creates a new object in space.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens when a star explodes?\n2. What is the new object created after a star explodes?\n3. What are the different types of objects that can be formed after a star explodes?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: When a star explodes, it releases a tremendous amount of energy in the form of light and heat. This explosion is called a supernova.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2: The new object created after a star explodes is called a remnant. This remnant can take different forms depending on the size of the star that exploded.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3: The different types of objects that can be formed after a star explodes include novae, red giants, supernovae, and white dwarfs.\n\nAnswering the original question: The intensely bright object formed after a star explodes is called a supernova. Therefore, the answer is C) supernova.",
