                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Read the question carefully and identify the key information. The question is asking for the name of the intensely bright object formed when a star explodes.\n\nStep 2: Review the answer choices and eliminate any that are clearly incorrect. Option B, red giant, is not the correct answer because red giants are formed when a star expands and cools, not when it explodes. Option D, white dwarf, is also not the correct answer because white dwarfs are formed when a star runs out of fuel and collapses, not when it explodes.\n\nStep 3: Consider the remaining answer choices and their definitions. A nova is a sudden brightening of a star caused by a thermonuclear explosion on its surface, but it is not necessarily the result of a star's complete destruction. A supernova, on the other hand, is a powerful and catastrophic explosion that occurs when a star has exhausted its fuel and collapses, resulting in the complete destruction of the star and the formation of a highly energetic and bright object.\n\nStep 4: Based on the definitions, the correct answer is C) supernova.\n\nStep 5: Double-check the answer to ensure it makes sense in the context of the question. Yes, the name of the intensely bright object formed when a star explodes is a supernova.",
