                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, where can we find the fossils of dinosaurs that lived millions of years ago?\n\nProfessor: The fossils of dinosaurs can be found in which of the following options: A) the water of oceans, B) the ice on ponds, C) the trunks of trees, or D) rocks in the ground?\n\nStudent: Oh, sorry. I didn't read the options carefully. So, the answer is D) rocks in the ground?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Fossils of dinosaurs are usually found in rocks in the ground. These rocks are called sedimentary rocks, and they are formed when layers of sediment, such as sand and mud, accumulate over time and harden into rock.\n\nStudent: How do the fossils get into the rocks?\n\nProfessor: When a dinosaur dies, its body may be buried by sediment, such as sand or mud. Over time, the soft tissues of the dinosaur decay and are replaced by minerals from the surrounding sediment. These minerals form a cast or mold of the dinosaur's bones, which eventually harden into rock.\n\nStudent: So, the fossils are actually the bones of the dinosaurs?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's right. Fossils are the remains of ancient organisms, such as dinosaurs, that have been preserved in rock. They can include bones, teeth, shells, and even footprints.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor. I understand now.",
                        "answers": [
