                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The rock cycle involves the formation and transformation of different types of rocks through various processes. Igneous rocks are formed when molten material (magma or lava) cools and solidifies.\n\nA) Cooling temperatures - This is the correct answer because igneous rocks form when molten material cools and solidifies.\n\nB) High pressure and heat - This is not the correct answer because these conditions are associated with the formation of metamorphic rocks, not igneous rocks.\n\nC) Weathering and erosion - This is not the correct answer because these processes break down rocks into smaller particles, which can eventually form sedimentary rocks, not igneous rocks.\n\nD) Compacted plant remains - This is not the correct answer because this process is associated with the formation of some types of sedimentary rocks, like coal, not igneous rocks.\n\nSo, the correct answer is A) cooling temperatures.",
                        "answers": [
