                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what weathering is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, weathering is the process by which rocks are broken down into smaller pieces by natural elements like wind, water, and ice.\n\nStudent: Okay, so which type of rock forms by this process?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is C) sedimentary rock. Sedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and cementation of small rock fragments, minerals, and organic matter that have been weathered and eroded from other rocks.\n\nStudent: Can you give an example of a sedimentary rock?\n\nProfessor: Sure, sandstone is a common example of a sedimentary rock. It is formed from the accumulation and cementation of sand-sized particles that have been weathered and eroded from other rocks.",
