                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The best description of wind energy is:\n\nB) renewable\n\nWind energy is considered renewable because it is generated by the natural movement of air currents, which are constantly replenished by the sun's heat. Unlike fossil fuels, which are finite and will eventually run out, wind energy is a sustainable source of power that can be harnessed for as long as the wind continues to blow. Therefore, option B is the correct answer. \n\nOption A (limited) is incorrect because wind energy is not limited in the sense that it is available in many parts of the world and can be harnessed to generate electricity. \n\nOption C (damaging) is incorrect because wind energy is generally considered to be a clean and environmentally friendly source of power, as it does not produce greenhouse gas emissions or other pollutants that can harm the environment. \n\nOption D (inexpensive) is incorrect because while wind energy can be cost-effective in the long run, it does require significant upfront investment in infrastructure and equipment, which can make it more expensive than other sources of energy in the short term.",
