                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Wind energy is a type of renewable energy that is generated by harnessing the power of wind to produce electricity.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is renewable energy?\nRenewable energy is energy that is generated from natural resources that are replenished over time, such as wind, solar, and hydro power.\n\n2. How is wind energy generated?\nWind energy is generated by using wind turbines to capture the kinetic energy of the wind and convert it into electricity.\n\n3. Is wind energy limited?\nNo, wind energy is not limited because wind is a natural resource that is constantly replenished.\n\n4. Is wind energy damaging?\nWind energy is generally considered to be a clean and environmentally friendly source of energy, but there are some concerns about the impact of wind turbines on wildlife and their habitats.\n\n5. Is wind energy inexpensive?\nWind energy can be relatively inexpensive compared to other sources of energy, but the cost can vary depending on factors such as the location and size of the wind farm.",
