                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain to me what wind energy is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, wind energy is a type of renewable energy that is generated by harnessing the power of wind to produce electricity.\n\nStudent: What do you mean by renewable energy?\n\nProfessor: Renewable energy is energy that comes from natural resources that are replenished over time, such as wind, solar, and hydro power. Unlike fossil fuels, which are finite and will eventually run out, renewable energy sources can be used indefinitely.\n\nStudent: So, is wind energy limited or renewable?\n\nProfessor: Wind energy is renewable, so the answer would be B.\n\nStudent: Why is wind energy renewable?\n\nProfessor: Wind energy is renewable because wind is a natural resource that is constantly replenished by the sun's heat and the Earth's rotation. As long as the sun shines and the Earth rotates, we will have wind to generate electricity.\n\nStudent: Is wind energy damaging to the environment?\n\nProfessor: Wind energy is generally considered to be one of the least damaging forms of energy production in terms of its impact on the environment. While there are some concerns about the impact of wind turbines on wildlife and their visual impact on the landscape, these impacts are generally considered to be minor compared to the environmental damage caused by fossil fuel extraction and combustion.\n\nStudent: Is wind energy expensive?\n\nProfessor: The cost of wind energy has been decreasing steadily over the past decade, and it is now one of the most cost-effective forms of renewable energy. While there are still some upfront costs associated with building and installing wind turbines, the long-term cost savings from using wind energy can be significant. So, the answer to the question would be D, inexpensive.",
