                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The first thing that would happen if there was too much rainfall is that the water would saturate the ground. This would lead to runoff and eventually flooding. However, this would not reduce the water level of the aquifer. In fact, it would likely raise the water level of the aquifer.\n\nThe second thing that could happen is that pollution could contaminate the water in the aquifer. This would make the water unsuitable for drinking and could lead to health problems.\n\nThe third thing that could happen is that irrigation could lead to the depletion of water in the aquifer. This is because irrigation removes water from the ground and uses it for crops. Over time, this could lead to a decrease in the water level of the aquifer.\n\nThe fourth thing that could happen is that evaporation could lead to the loss of water in the aquifer. This is because water evaporates when it is exposed to the air. Over time, this could lead to a decrease in the water level of the aquifer.\n\nThe correct answer is C) irrigation.",
