                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the meaning of adaptation.\n2. Understand the impact of habitat destruction on organisms.\n3. Analyze each option and determine which one is most likely an adaptation resulting from habitat destruction.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Adaptation refers to the process by which organisms change over time to better suit their environment and increase their chances of survival.\n2. Habitat destruction can have a significant impact on organisms, as it can alter their environment and reduce the availability of resources they need to survive. This can lead to changes in behavior, physical characteristics, and other adaptations that help them cope with the new conditions.\n3. Analyzing the options:\nA) A bird building its nest in a water tower may be an adaptation to urbanization, but not necessarily habitat destruction.\nB) A rabbit's fur turning white in the winter is a natural adaptation to seasonal changes, not habitat destruction.\nC) A lizard shedding its skin is a natural process that helps them grow and replace damaged skin, not an adaptation resulting from habitat destruction.\nD) A salmon swimming upstream is a natural adaptation to their life cycle and reproductive needs, not habitat destruction.\n\nTherefore, the most likely adaptation resulting from habitat destruction is not listed among the options.",
