                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Cars are a major source of air pollution, emitting pollutants such as carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides, and particulate matter.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the main causes of air pollution from cars?\n2. How do longer routes, larger cars, fewer car trips, and smaller tires affect air pollution from cars?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The main causes of air pollution from cars are emissions from the engine and exhaust system, as well as dust and debris from tires and brakes.\n2. Driving a longer route would increase air pollution from cars, as it would result in more emissions and use more fuel. Purchasing a larger car would also increase air pollution, as larger cars typically have larger engines and emit more pollutants. Taking fewer car trips would reduce air pollution, as there would be fewer cars on the road emitting pollutants. Using smaller tires would not have a significant impact on air pollution from cars, as the emissions from the engine and exhaust system are the main sources of pollution. \n\nTherefore, the answer is C) take fewer car trips.",
