                    {
                        "id": "f6696f26-650a-4039-ac88-a22ec485c0df",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The Earth's atmosphere is divided into four main layers based on temperature changes: troposphere, stratosphere, mesosphere, and thermosphere. The temperature decreases as altitude increases in the troposphere, but increases in the stratosphere and thermosphere before decreasing again in the mesosphere.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the temperature trend in the troposphere?\n2. What is the temperature trend in the stratosphere?\n3. What is the temperature trend in the mesosphere?\n4. What is the temperature trend in the thermosphere?\n5. At what altitude is the summit of Mount Everest located?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The temperature decreases as altitude increases in the troposphere.\n2. The temperature increases as altitude increases in the stratosphere.\n3. The temperature decreases as altitude increases in the mesosphere.\n4. The temperature increases as altitude increases in the thermosphere.\n5. The summit of Mount Everest is located at an altitude of 8,848 meters (29,029 feet).\n\nUsing the knowledge and answers above, we can determine that the summit of Mount Everest is located in the troposphere, as the temperature decreases as altitude increases in this layer. Therefore, the answer is D) troposphere.",
