                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Recall the layers of the atmosphere and their characteristics.\n- Troposphere: lowest layer, where weather occurs, temperature decreases with altitude\n- Stratosphere: contains the ozone layer, temperature increases with altitude\n- Mesosphere: middle layer, temperature decreases with altitude\n- Thermosphere: highest layer, temperature increases with altitude due to absorption of solar radiation\n\nStep 2: Use the information given in the question to eliminate some options.\n- The temperature on Mount Everest decreases with altitude, so it cannot be in the stratosphere where the temperature increases with altitude.\n- The temperature also cannot be increasing with altitude, so it cannot be in the thermosphere.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer.\n- The only two options left are the troposphere and the mesosphere.\n- Since Mount Everest is a terrestrial mountain and not in space, it is safe to assume that the summit is still within the Earth's atmosphere.\n- Therefore, the summit of Mount Everest is in the mesosphere, where the temperature decreases with altitude.\n\nAnswer: A) mesosphere",
