                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking how ocean currents, specifically the Gulf Stream, affect world climate. \n\nOption A states that ocean currents spread plant and animal life over a wider area. While this may be true, it is not directly related to how ocean currents affect world climate. \n\nOption B states that ocean currents ensure ocean density is not the same globally. Again, while this may be true, it is not directly related to how ocean currents affect world climate. \n\nOption C states that ocean currents carry sediment from rivers and inland basins. This may have some impact on climate, but it is not a significant factor compared to other effects of ocean currents. \n\nOption D states that ocean currents transfer heat to and from various regions. This is the correct answer. The Gulf Stream, for example, carries warm water from the Gulf of Mexico to the North Atlantic, which helps to moderate the climate in Europe. Without the Gulf Stream, Europe would be much colder. Similarly, other ocean currents help to distribute heat around the world, affecting climate patterns. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) transferring heat to and from various regions.",
