                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how ocean currents affect world climate?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Ocean currents, like the Gulf Stream, transfer heat to and from various regions, which affects the world climate.\n\nStudent: How does transferring heat affect the world climate?\n\nProfessor: Well, the transfer of heat from one region to another can cause changes in temperature and precipitation patterns, which can have a significant impact on the climate.\n\nStudent: Does the Gulf Stream affect the density of the ocean?\n\nProfessor: Yes, it does. The Gulf Stream is a warm current that flows from the Gulf of Mexico to the North Atlantic, and it helps to ensure that ocean density is not the same globally.\n\nStudent: How does the Gulf Stream ensure that ocean density is not the same globally?\n\nProfessor: The Gulf Stream carries warm water from the tropics to the North Atlantic, where it cools and sinks to the bottom of the ocean. This process helps to maintain the global ocean circulation system, which is important for regulating the Earth's climate.\n\nStudent: Does the Gulf Stream affect plant and animal life?\n\nProfessor: Yes, it does. Ocean currents like the Gulf Stream can spread plant and animal life over a wider area, which can have both positive and negative effects on ecosystems.\n\nStudent: Can ocean currents carry sediment from rivers and inland basins?\n\nProfessor: Yes, they can. Ocean currents can transport sediment from rivers and inland basins to the ocean, where it can affect the distribution of nutrients and the formation of coastal habitats.",
