                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: When cold air is at the tops of mountains, it is at a higher altitude than the surrounding areas.\n\nStep 2: Due to gravity, air tends to flow from areas of higher pressure to areas of lower pressure.\n\nStep 3: At higher altitudes, the air pressure is lower than at lower altitudes.\n\nStep 4: Therefore, the cold air at the tops of mountains will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys.\n\nStep 5: Option A is the correct answer.\n\nStep 6: Option B is incorrect because the air flows from higher pressure to lower pressure.\n\nStep 7: Option C is partially correct, as cold air is indeed less dense than warm air, but this is not the reason why it flows toward valleys.\n\nStep 8: Option D is incorrect, as cold air still contains oxygen atoms.",
