                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the main idea of the question.\nThe question is asking about the behavior of cold air at the tops of mountains.\n\nStep 2: Eliminate obviously incorrect options.\nOption D, \"is considered to be free of oxygen atoms,\" is not a logical or relevant answer to the question, so it can be eliminated.\n\nStep 3: Consider the remaining options.\nOption A, \"will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys,\" seems like a logical answer because cold air is denser than warm air, so it will tend to sink and flow downhill towards areas of lower pressure. Option B, \"will flow toward areas of higher pressure in valleys,\" is not a logical answer because cold air is denser than warm air, so it will not tend to rise and flow uphill towards areas of higher pressure. Option C, \"is considered to be less dense than warmer air,\" is a true statement, but it does not directly answer the question about the behavior of cold air at the tops of mountains.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best answer.\nBased on the logic and information presented, the best answer is A) will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys.",
