                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking for the similarity between two processes: tree roots growing into rock and water freezing in the cracks of rock. \n\nTo determine the similarity, we need to analyze the characteristics of each process. \n\nTree roots growing into rock: This process involves the roots of a tree growing into the cracks and crevices of a rock. As the roots grow, they can exert pressure on the rock, causing it to break apart. \n\nWater freezing in the cracks of rock: This process involves water seeping into the cracks and crevices of a rock. When the temperature drops, the water freezes and expands, causing the rock to break apart. \n\nNow, we need to compare the two processes and determine the similarity. \n\nA) Both are forces: This is true, as both processes involve a force exerted on the rock. In the case of tree roots, it is the force of the roots growing and expanding. In the case of water freezing, it is the force of the expanding ice. \n\nB) Both affect weather: This is not true, as neither process directly affects the weather. \n\nC) Both form new kinds of rock: This is not true, as neither process forms new kinds of rock. \n\nD) Both are forms of weathering: This is true, as both processes are examples of physical weathering, which involves the breakdown of rock due to physical forces. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Both are forms of weathering.",
