                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the similarity between tree roots growing into rock and water freezing in the cracks of rock?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Tree roots growing into rock and water freezing in the cracks of rock are two different processes.\n- We need to identify what they have in common.\n- Tree roots growing into rock can exert pressure and force on the rock, causing it to break apart.\n- Water freezing in the cracks of rock can also exert pressure and force on the rock, causing it to break apart.\n- Therefore, both processes involve the breaking apart of rock due to external forces.\n- This is a form of weathering, which is the breakdown of rocks and minerals by physical, chemical, or biological processes.\n- Therefore, the answer is D) Both are forms of weathering.\n\nAnswer: D) Both are forms of weathering.",
