                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how hurricanes can be predicted to occur in the Northern Hemisphere between June and November?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Hurricanes are formed over warm ocean waters and typically occur during the summer and fall months. Meteorologists use various tools such as satellite imagery, computer models, and weather balloons to track and predict the formation and movement of hurricanes.\n\nStudent: How about volcanic eruptions? How can they be predicted?\n\nProfessor: Volcanic eruptions are more difficult to predict than hurricanes. However, scientists can monitor volcanic activity by measuring gas emissions, seismic activity, and changes in the shape of the volcano. This data can help them make predictions about when an eruption may occur.\n\nStudent: What about tsunamis? How can they be predicted?\n\nProfessor: Tsunamis can be caused by earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, or landslides that occur under the ocean. Scientists use seismometers to detect earthquakes and monitor the movement of tectonic plates. They can also use ocean buoys to detect changes in sea level that may indicate the formation of a tsunami.\n\nStudent: And finally, how can asteroid impacts be predicted?\n\nProfessor: Asteroid impacts are rare but can be catastrophic. Scientists use telescopes to track the movement of asteroids and predict their path. They can also use computer models to simulate the impact of an asteroid and determine the potential damage it could cause. However, predicting the exact time and location of an asteroid impact is still a challenge.",
