                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) The supply of warm, moist air decreases.\n\nExplanation:\nHurricanes are fueled by warm, moist air over the ocean. As the hurricane moves over land, it loses its source of warm, moist air and begins to weaken. The land surface is not able to provide the same amount of heat and moisture as the ocean, which causes the hurricane to lose energy. Therefore, the supply of warm, moist air decreases, which is the best explanation for why the force of a hurricane diminishes as it moves over land. \n\nOption A is incorrect because the development of a high pressure area does not explain why the force of a hurricane diminishes over land. Option B is incorrect because the sea level rising on the coast is not related to the force of a hurricane diminishing over land. Option C is incorrect because the winds of a hurricane do not start to spin clockwise as it moves over land.",
