                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to convert the temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit to better understand it. To do this, we can use the formula F = (C x 1.8) + 32, where F is the temperature in Fahrenheit and C is the temperature in Celsius.\n\nF = (32 x 1.8) + 32\nF = 57.6 + 32\nF = 89.6\n\nSo, the temperature outside is 89.6\u00b0F. This is a relatively high temperature, so we can eliminate options A and B, which describe cooler weather. Option D also doesn't fit, as spring weather can vary widely and may not necessarily be warm.\n\nTherefore, the most likely answer is C) hot, sunny summer weather.",
