                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The student hears on the radio that the outside temperature is 32\u00b0C. To determine what type of weather the student can expect when she steps outside, we need to convert the temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit. \n\nTo convert Celsius to Fahrenheit, we can use the formula: F = (C x 1.8) + 32, where F is the temperature in Fahrenheit and C is the temperature in Celsius. \n\nSo, F = (32 x 1.8) + 32 = 89.6\u00b0F. \n\nTherefore, the student can expect hot, sunny summer weather when she steps outside. \n\nThe answer is C) hot, sunny summer weather.",
