                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the types of energy mentioned in the question.\n2. Determine which type of energy was present in the breakfast.\n3. Determine which type of energy is used in bicycling.\n4. Match the two types of energy to identify the energy transformation that occurred.\n\nAnswer:\n1. The types of energy mentioned in the question are radiant, nuclear, chemical, and mechanical.\n2. The breakfast that the student ate most likely contained chemical energy, as it was likely made up of food that the student consumed.\n3. Bicycling requires mechanical energy, as it involves the movement of the bicycle and the rider's body.\n4. The energy transformation that occurred was from chemical energy (in the breakfast) to mechanical energy (used in bicycling). Therefore, the correct answer is D) chemical to mechanical.",
