                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the process that is occurring when a lightbulb is lit.\n- When a lightbulb is lit, electrical energy is being converted into another form of energy.\n\nStep 2: Determine what form of energy is being produced by the lightbulb.\n- The form of energy being produced by the lightbulb is light energy.\n\nStep 3: Identify which of the answer choices represents a form of energy that is not being produced by the lightbulb.\n- Chemical energy is not being produced by the lightbulb.\n- Magnetic energy is not being produced by the lightbulb.\n- Heat energy is being produced by the lightbulb, but it is not the primary form of energy being produced.\n- Mechanical energy is not being produced by the lightbulb.\n\nStep 4: Choose the answer that represents the correct form of energy being produced by the lightbulb and the incorrect form of energy.\n- The correct form of energy being produced by the lightbulb is light energy.\n- The incorrect form of energy is chemical energy, magnetic energy, heat energy, and mechanical energy.\n- Therefore, the answer is A) chemical energy.",
