                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) heat energy.\n\nExplanation:\n\nWhen a lightbulb is lit, electrical energy flows through the filament, which is a thin wire inside the bulb. The filament resists the flow of electricity, causing it to heat up. As the filament heats up, it begins to glow and emit light. However, not all of the electrical energy is converted into light energy. Some of it is lost as heat energy, which is why lightbulbs get hot when they are on for a long time. Therefore, the correct answer is C) heat energy.",
