                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What type of energy is produced when electrical energy is converted into light energy in a lit lightbulb?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- We know that when a lightbulb is lit, electrical energy is converted into light energy.\n- We need to identify the type of energy that is produced in addition to light energy.\n- Option A, chemical energy, does not seem relevant to the process of converting electrical energy into light energy in a lightbulb.\n- Option B, magnetic energy, also does not seem relevant to the process.\n- Option C, heat energy, is a possibility since lightbulbs do produce some heat when they are lit. However, the primary output of a lightbulb is light energy, not heat energy.\n- Option D, mechanical energy, does not seem relevant to the process either.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is C) heat energy, although it is not the primary output of a lightbulb.\n\nAnswer: C) heat energy",
                        "answers": [
