                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, the electric fan converts electricity into mechanical energy. This is the energy that makes the blades of the fan move. \n\nNext, the fan blades moving through the air create a wind. This wind is created by the fan blades moving through the air, which is a form of mechanical energy. \n\nThe wind created by the fan blades moving through the air can create a cooling effect on the skin. This is because when the wind blows, it evaporates the sweat on the skin, which cools the body. The wind created by the fan can also help to circulate the air in a room, which can also help to cool the room. \n\nSo, in summary, the electric fan converts electricity into mechanical energy, which is then converted into heat energy, sound energy, and mechanical energy.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "5a5101ae-7fab-4bcc-b69e-eed0f382d7c5",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
