                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "we need to understand how an electric fan works. An electric fan has a motor that converts electrical energy into mechanical energy, which is used to rotate the blades of the fan. As the blades rotate, they move the air around, creating a flow of air that can be felt as a breeze. This means that an electric fan converts electricity into mechanical energy and also into movement of air, which can be considered a form of kinetic energy.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) heat energy, sound energy, and mechanical energy only. While there may be some minor conversion of electrical energy into other forms (such as electromagnetic radiation), the primary forms of energy that an electric fan produces are heat energy (due to the resistance of the motor and other components), sound energy (due to the noise produced by the motor and the movement of air), and mechanical energy (due to the rotation of the blades). There is no significant conversion of chemical energy involved in the operation of an electric fan.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f96799a2-5158-4e35-971e-9f7231ad83f9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
