                        "cot": "\nA) tidal energy and hydropower: Tidal energy is produced by the surge of ocean waters during the rise and fall of tides. Hydropower is produced by the force of flowing water such as a river or stream. These two resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.\nB) geothermal energy and hydropower: Geothermal energy is produced by the Earth's internal heat while hydropower is produced by the force of flowing water such as a river or stream. These two resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.\nC) wind energy and tidal energy: Wind energy is produced by the wind while tidal energy is produced by the surge of ocean waters during the rise and fall of tides. These two resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.\nD) geothermal energy and wind energy: Geothermal energy is produced by the Earth's internal heat while wind energy is produced by the wind. These two resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.",
