                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which alternative energy resources use gravitational energy to make electricity.\n\nStep 2: Define gravitational energy\nGravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field.\n\nStep 3: Identify the options\nA) tidal energy and hydropower\nB) geothermal energy and hydropower\nC) wind energy and tidal energy\nD) geothermal energy and wind energy\n\nStep 4: Determine which options use gravitational energy\nTidal energy and hydropower both use the gravitational energy of water to generate electricity. As the tides rise and fall, or water flows downstream, the potential energy stored in the water due to its position in the Earth's gravitational field is converted into kinetic energy, which is then used to turn turbines and generate electricity. Therefore, option A is the correct answer.\n\nGeothermal energy and wind energy do not use gravitational energy to generate electricity. Geothermal energy is generated by the heat of the Earth's core, while wind energy is generated by the kinetic energy of moving air. Option B and D are incorrect. Option C is incorrect because wind energy does not use gravitational energy.",
                        "answers": [
