                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you repeat the question, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Which alternative energy resources use gravitational energy to make electricity?\n\nStudent: What do you mean by gravitational energy?\n\nProfessor: Gravitational energy is the energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field. In this case, we're talking about the energy stored in water due to its position above the ground.\n\nStudent: Okay, so which options use this type of energy?\n\nProfessor: The options are A) tidal energy and hydropower.\n\nStudent: How do they use gravitational energy?\n\nProfessor: Tidal energy uses the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun to create tides in the ocean. These tides are then used to turn turbines and generate electricity. Hydropower, on the other hand, uses the gravitational energy of water stored in dams. The water is released from the dam and flows through turbines, generating electricity.\n\nStudent: So, the correct answer is A?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Tidal energy and hydropower both use gravitational energy to make electricity.",
