                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: A mirror is a smooth, highly polished surface that reflects light.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens when light hits a mirror?\n2. How does a mirror reflect light?\n3. What are the possible outcomes when light hits a surface?\n\nAnswers:\n1. When light hits a mirror, it interacts with the surface of the mirror and changes direction.\n2. A mirror reflects light by bouncing it back at the same angle as it hit the surface.\n3. When light hits a surface, it can be refracted (bent), reflected, absorbed, or transmitted. \n\nTherefore, the answer to the original question is B) reflected. When light hits a mirror, most of the light is reflected.",
