                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the concept of potential energy.\n2. Identify the factors that affect potential energy.\n3. Analyze the roller coaster's motion and position.\n4. Determine the point where the front car of the coaster has the greatest potential energy.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its position or configuration. It is the energy that an object has because of its position relative to other objects.\n2. The factors that affect potential energy are the object's mass, height, and the acceleration due to gravity.\n3. As the roller coaster climbs up the highest hill on its track, it gains height and potential energy. At the top of the hill, the roller coaster has the most potential energy because it is at its highest point.\n4. Therefore, the answer is B) at the top of the highest hill.",
