                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The potential energy of an object is determined by its position relative to a reference point. In this case, the reference point can be chosen to be the bottom of the track. As the roller coaster climbs up the hill, it gains potential energy because it is moving farther away from the reference point. Therefore, the front car of the coaster will have its greatest potential energy at the top of the highest hill (option B), where it is farthest from the reference point. \n\nOption A can be eliminated because the front car would have the least potential energy at the bottom of the hill, where it is closest to the reference point. Option C can also be eliminated because the roller coaster has not yet gained any height or potential energy at the start of the track. Option D can be eliminated because the roller coaster would have lost most of its potential energy by the end of the track, as it would have descended back down to the reference point.",
