                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Radio waves and infrared waves are both types of electromagnetic waves that travel through space at the speed of light, which is approximately 299,792,458 meters per second.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are radio waves?\n2. What are infrared waves?\n3. How are radio waves and infrared waves similar?\n4. How are radio waves and infrared waves different?\n5. Does the frequency of a wave affect its speed?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Radio waves are a type of electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths ranging from about one millimeter to 100 kilometers. They are used for communication, such as in radio and television broadcasting, cell phone networks, and satellite communications.\n2. Infrared waves are a type of electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths ranging from about 700 nanometers to 1 millimeter. They are used for heating, such as in infrared heaters and ovens, and for sensing, such as in thermal imaging cameras.\n3. Both radio waves and infrared waves are types of electromagnetic waves that travel through space at the speed of light.\n4. Radio waves and infrared waves differ in their wavelengths and frequencies. Radio waves have longer wavelengths and lower frequencies than infrared waves.\n5. The speed of a wave is determined by its wavelength and frequency. In general, waves with longer wavelengths and lower frequencies travel faster than waves with shorter wavelengths and higher frequencies. However, for electromagnetic waves in a vacuum, such as radio waves and infrared waves, the speed is always the same, regardless of their frequency. Therefore, the answer is C) They both travel at the same speed.",
