                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, the workers need to lift the piano up to the window. This could potentially be done with a wheel and axle, but it would require a lot of effort and coordination from the workers. An inclined plane could also be used to help lift the piano, but it would need to be a very long and gradual slope to avoid damaging the piano.\n\nOnce the piano is at the window, the workers need to lower it down to the ground. This is where a pulley would be the best tool to use. By attaching the piano to a rope or cable that runs through a pulley, the workers can use their own weight to slowly and safely lower the piano to the ground.\n\nA wedge would not be useful in this situation, as it is designed to split or separate objects, not to lift or lower them. Therefore, the best tool for the workers to use in this scenario would be a pulley.",
