                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the best tool to help workers lower a piano from a second-floor window?\n\nTo lower the piano from the second floor of a building, the workers need a tool that can help them move the piano down through the window. The tool that would be best for this task is one that can reduce the amount of force needed to move the piano and make it easier to control its descent. \n\nA) Wheel and axle: This tool is not suitable for lowering a piano from a window as it is designed to help move objects horizontally, not vertically.\n\nB) Inclined plane: This tool could be used to create a ramp to slide the piano down, but it would require a lot of space and may not be practical for a second-floor window.\n\nC) Pulley: This tool is the best option for lowering the piano from the window. It can reduce the amount of force needed to move the piano and make it easier to control its descent.\n\nD) Wedge: This tool is not suitable for lowering a piano from a window as it is designed to split objects apart, not move them vertically.\n\nTherefore, the best tool to help the workers lower the piano from the window is C) pulley.",
