                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The workers need to lower the piano from the second floor of a building through a window because it is too wide to fit through the door.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a wheel and axle?\n2. How does a wheel and axle work?\n3. What is an inclined plane?\n4. How does an inclined plane work?\n5. What is a pulley?\n6. How does a pulley work?\n7. What is a wedge?\n8. How does a wedge work?\n9. Which tool would be best to help the workers lower the piano from the window?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A wheel and axle is a simple machine consisting of a wheel attached to a smaller axle.\n2. A wheel and axle work by rotating the wheel around the axle, which allows for the transfer of force and the ability to lift or move heavy objects.\n3. An inclined plane is a flat surface that is angled, allowing for easier movement of objects up or down.\n4. An inclined plane works by reducing the amount of force needed to move an object by increasing the distance over which the force is applied.\n5. A pulley is a simple machine consisting of a wheel with a groove in its rim, which is used to change the direction of a force applied to a rope or cable.\n6. A pulley works by allowing the force to be redirected, making it easier to lift or move heavy objects.\n7. A wedge is a simple machine consisting of a triangular-shaped object that is used to split or lift objects.\n8. A wedge works by applying force to a small area, which increases the pressure and allows for the object to be split or lifted.\n9. The best tool to help the workers lower the piano from the window would be a pulley, as it would allow them to redirect the force and make it easier to lift or move the heavy object. Therefore, the answer is C) pulley.",
