                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain the question again?\n\nProfessor: Sure, a group of workers needs to move a piano from the second floor of a building. The piano is too wide to fit through the door, so they will lower the piano to the ground through a window. Which tool would be best to help the workers lower the piano from the window?\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand the question now. Can you explain what a wheel and axle is?\n\nProfessor: A wheel and axle is a simple machine that consists of a wheel attached to a smaller axle. When the wheel turns, it rotates the axle, which can be used to lift or move heavy objects.\n\nStudent: And what about an inclined plane?\n\nProfessor: An inclined plane is a flat surface that is sloped. It allows objects to be moved up or down with less force than it would take to lift them straight up.\n\nStudent: What is a pulley?\n\nProfessor: A pulley is a simple machine that consists of a wheel with a groove in it and a rope or cable that runs through the groove. When the rope is pulled, the wheel turns and can be used to lift or move heavy objects.\n\nStudent: And finally, what is a wedge?\n\nProfessor: A wedge is a simple machine that is shaped like a triangle. It is used to split or lift objects by applying force to the wide end of the wedge.\n\nStudent: Okay, I think I understand now. So, which tool would be best to help the workers lower the piano from the window?\n\nProfessor: Based on the situation, a pulley would be the best tool to help the workers lower the piano from the window. It would allow them to use less force and make the process easier and safer.",
