                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The characteristic that all vertebrates share is having a backbone. This means that they all have a series of bones called vertebrae that run down their back and protect their spinal cord. Option C is the correct answer. \n\nOption A is incorrect because not all vertebrates lay eggs. Some give birth to live young, such as most mammals. \n\nOption B is incorrect because not all vertebrates have feathers. Feathers are a unique characteristic of birds. \n\nOption D is incorrect because not all vertebrates are warm-blooded. Some are cold-blooded, such as reptiles and fish.",
