                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Vertebrates are animals that have a backbone or spinal column. They are classified into five groups: fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds, and mammals.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a vertebrate?\n2. What are the five groups of vertebrates?\n3. What characteristic do all vertebrates share?\n\nAnswering the sub-questions:\n1. A vertebrate is an animal that has a backbone or spinal column.\n2. The five groups of vertebrates are fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds, and mammals.\n3. The characteristic that all vertebrates share is that they have a backbone or spinal column.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nC) They all have a backbone.",
