                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I read that birds, mammals, and reptiles are all vertebrates. Can you tell me which characteristic they all share?\n\nProfessor: Sure, all vertebrates share a common characteristic. Can you tell me which of the options you think it is?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure, but I think it might be that they all lay eggs.\n\nProfessor: That's a good guess, but not quite right. Some vertebrates do lay eggs, but not all of them. Can you think of any other options?\n\nStudent: Hmm, maybe they all have feathers?\n\nProfessor: No, not all vertebrates have feathers. That's a characteristic that only birds have. Let me give you a hint. Think about the word \"vertebrate.\" What does that word mean?\n\nStudent: Oh, I know! It means they all have a backbone!\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct! All vertebrates have a backbone, which is also called a spinal column. This is what sets them apart from invertebrates, which don't have a backbone.",
