                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that the parts that capture sunlight are called chloroplasts. \n\nNext, we know that chloroplasts are responsible for photosynthesis, which is the process by which plants make food. \n\nFinally, we know that photosynthesis requires sunlight, so the parts that capture sunlight (chloroplasts) will be found in the parts of the plant that are most exposed to sunlight. \n\nTherefore, the answer is C) leaves. Leaves are the primary site of photosynthesis in most plants, and they are typically the most exposed part of the plant to sunlight.",
