                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight, carbon dioxide, and water to produce glucose (sugar) and oxygen.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is photosynthesis?\n2. What are the inputs of photosynthesis?\n3. What are the outputs of photosynthesis?\n4. Which of the outputs is a substance produced by plants during photosynthesis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight, carbon dioxide, and water to produce glucose (sugar) and oxygen.\n2. The inputs of photosynthesis are sunlight, carbon dioxide, and water.\n3. The outputs of photosynthesis are glucose (sugar) and oxygen.\n4. The substance produced by plants during photosynthesis is sugar (glucose). \n\nTherefore, the answer is D) sugar.",
