                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I have a question about photosynthesis. I learned that plants survive through this process, but I'm not sure what substance they produce. Can you help me with that?\n\nProfessor: Sure, I'd be happy to help. Which substance are you referring to?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. Can you tell me which substance plants produce during photosynthesis?\n\nProfessor: Yes, plants produce sugar during photosynthesis.\n\nStudent: Oh, okay. How do they produce sugar?\n\nProfessor: During photosynthesis, plants use energy from sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose, which is a type of sugar.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. So, why do plants need sugar?\n\nProfessor: Sugar is a source of energy for plants. They use it to fuel their growth and other metabolic processes.\n\nStudent: I see. And what happens to the oxygen that's produced during photosynthesis?\n\nProfessor: The oxygen is released into the atmosphere as a byproduct of photosynthesis. It's what we breathe in to survive.",
