                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Plants undergo photosynthesis to produce their own food. This process requires sunlight, water, and a substance from the air.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is photosynthesis?\n2. What are the requirements for photosynthesis?\n3. What substance from the air do plants need for photosynthesis?\n4. What happens to the substance from the air during photosynthesis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose (sugar) and oxygen.\n2. The requirements for photosynthesis are sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide.\n3. Plants need carbon dioxide from the air for photosynthesis.\n4. During photosynthesis, carbon dioxide is converted into glucose, while oxygen is released as a byproduct.\n\nAnswer to original question: A) carbon dioxide.",
