                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking about how people obtain energy and nutrients. \n\nOption A, breathing clean air, is not directly related to obtaining energy and nutrients. While oxygen is necessary for cellular respiration, which produces energy, it is not the only source of energy and nutrients.\n\nOption B, exercising and playing, can help maintain a healthy body and improve overall energy levels, but it is not the primary way people obtain energy and nutrients.\n\nOption C, getting plenty of rest, is important for overall health and energy levels, but it does not directly provide energy and nutrients.\n\nOption D, eating healthy food, is the correct answer. Food provides the body with the necessary nutrients and energy to function properly. Nutrients such as carbohydrates, proteins, and fats are broken down during digestion and used by the body for energy and other functions. Vitamins and minerals are also obtained through food and are necessary for various bodily processes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) eating healthy food.",
