                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Crickets are insects that require a source of energy to survive. They are known to be herbivores, meaning they feed on plants. Sunlight is also important for the growth of plants.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What do crickets eat?\n2. What is the purpose of the water in the tank?\n3. What is the purpose of the soil and plants in the tank?\n4. How do plants obtain energy?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Crickets are herbivores and feed on plants.\n2. The water in the tank is likely for the crickets to drink and for the plants to absorb.\n3. The soil and plants in the tank provide a food source for the crickets.\n4. Plants obtain energy through photosynthesis, which requires sunlight. Therefore, the crickets ultimately gain their energy from the sunlight that the plants use to grow. \n\nAnswer: D) the sunlight.",
